{
  "id": "cb14",
  "title": "Reports",
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "cb14-l1",
      "title": "The Printer",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "Most COBOL output went to the line printer: a file ASSIGNed TO PRINTER. Each WRITE prints one line, here in the output box.",
        "WRITE … AFTER ADVANCING 2 LINES leaves an empty line first; AFTER ADVANCING PAGE starts a new page (here: an empty line). That's how reports got their spacing.",
        "Report lines are built in WORKING-STORAGE and written with WRITE PRINT-LINE FROM HEADING-1."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.",
          "       PROGRAM-ID. PRINTER.",
          "       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.",
          "       INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.",
          "       FILE-CONTROL.",
          "           SELECT REPORT-FILE ASSIGN TO PRINTER.",
          "       DATA DIVISION.",
          "       FILE SECTION.",
          "       FD REPORT-FILE.",
          "       01 PRINT-LINE     PIC X(40).",
          "       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.",
          "       01 HEADING-1      PIC X(30) VALUE \"CUSTOMER LIST\".",
          "       01 HEADING-2      PIC X(30) VALUE \"NO.   NAME\".",
          "       PROCEDURE DIVISION.",
          "           OPEN OUTPUT REPORT-FILE.",
          "           WRITE PRINT-LINE FROM HEADING-1.",
          "           WRITE PRINT-LINE FROM HEADING-2 AFTER ADVANCING 2 LINES.",
          "           WRITE PRINT-LINE FROM \"-----------------\".",
          "           CLOSE REPORT-FILE.",
          "           STOP RUN."
        ],
        "output": [
          "CUSTOMER LIST",
          "",
          "NO.   NAME",
          "-----------------"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "cb14-l1-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does ASSIGN TO PRINTER do?",
          "options": [
            "Every WRITE prints a line on the printer",
            "Saves the file on disk",
            "Reads from the printer",
            "Nothing"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Here, the printed lines show up in the output."
        },
        {
          "id": "cb14-l1-e2",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does AFTER ADVANCING 2 LINES do?",
          "options": [
            "Moves the paper 2 lines, leaving one empty line, then prints",
            "Prints 2 copies",
            "Prints 2 lines of text",
            "Skips 2 records"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Spacing for headings and totals."
        },
        {
          "id": "cb14-l1-e3",
          "type": "fill_blank",
          "prompt": "Print a heading.",
          "code": [
            "           WRITE PRINT-LINE ___ HEADING-1."
          ],
          "options": [
            "FROM",
            "TO",
            "WITH",
            "AS"
          ],
          "answer": "FROM",
          "explanation": "WRITE … FROM …."
        },
        {
          "id": "cb14-l1-e4",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does AFTER ADVANCING PAGE do on a real printer?",
          "options": [
            "Starts a new page",
            "Prints the page number",
            "Prints every page",
            "Nothing"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Here it's shown as an empty line."
        },
        {
          "id": "cb14-l1-e5",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "Why build report lines in WORKING-STORAGE?",
          "options": [
            "They have VALUEs and edited fields; the print record is just the line to write",
            "Records can't be printed",
            "WORKING-STORAGE prints faster",
            "It's required"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Many layouts, one print record."
        },
        {
          "id": "cb14-l1-e6",
          "type": "order_lines",
          "prompt": "Put the steps in order.",
          "lines": [
            "           OPEN OUTPUT REPORT-FILE.",
            "           WRITE PRINT-LINE FROM HEADING-1.",
            "           CLOSE REPORT-FILE."
          ],
          "answer": [
            "           OPEN OUTPUT REPORT-FILE.",
            "           WRITE PRINT-LINE FROM HEADING-1.",
            "           CLOSE REPORT-FILE."
          ],
          "explanation": "Open, write, close."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cb14-l2",
      "title": "Detail Lines",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "A report has headings at the top and a detail line for each record. The detail line is a group with edited fields: name, city and the balance as money.",
        "For each record READ, MOVE the input fields into the detail line, then WRITE it. The columns line up by themselves.",
        "This read-move-write loop is the heart of thousands of real COBOL programs."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.",
          "       PROGRAM-ID. CUSTLIST.",
          "       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.",
          "       INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.",
          "       FILE-CONTROL.",
          "           SELECT CUST-FILE ASSIGN TO CUSTOMERS.",
          "           SELECT REPORT-FILE ASSIGN TO PRINTER.",
          "       DATA DIVISION.",
          "       FILE SECTION.",
          "       FD CUST-FILE.",
          "       01 CUST-REC.",
          "          05 CUST-NO      PIC 9(5).",
          "          05 CUST-NAME    PIC X(12).",
          "          05 CUST-CITY    PIC X(10).",
          "          05 CUST-BAL     PIC 9(5)V99.",
          "       FD REPORT-FILE.",
          "       01 PRINT-LINE     PIC X(40).",
          "       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.",
          "       01 EOF-FLAG       PIC X VALUE \"N\".",
          "          88 END-OF-FILE VALUE \"Y\".",
          "       01 DETAIL-LINE.",
          "          05 D-NAME       PIC X(13).",
          "          05 D-CITY       PIC X(11).",
          "          05 D-BAL        PIC $$$,$$9.99.",
          "       PROCEDURE DIVISION.",
          "       MAIN.",
          "           OPEN INPUT CUST-FILE OUTPUT REPORT-FILE.",
          "           WRITE PRINT-LINE FROM \"NAME         CITY          BALANCE\".",
          "           PERFORM UNTIL END-OF-FILE",
          "               READ CUST-FILE",
          "                   AT END SET END-OF-FILE TO TRUE",
          "                   NOT AT END PERFORM PRINT-DETAIL",
          "               END-READ",
          "           END-PERFORM.",
          "           CLOSE CUST-FILE REPORT-FILE.",
          "           STOP RUN.",
          "       PRINT-DETAIL.",
          "           MOVE CUST-NAME TO D-NAME.",
          "           MOVE CUST-CITY TO D-CITY.",
          "           MOVE CUST-BAL  TO D-BAL.",
          "           WRITE PRINT-LINE FROM DETAIL-LINE."
        ],
        "output": [
          "NAME         CITY          BALANCE",
          "GRACE HOPPER NEW YORK    $2,500.00",
          "ADA LOVELACE LONDON      $1,815.36",
          "JOHN BACKUS  PHILADELPH    $120.00",
          "LINUS T.     HELSINKI        $9.99"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "cb14-l2-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What's a detail line?",
          "options": [
            "The line printed for each record",
            "The first line of a report",
            "The total at the end",
            "A line with details about the program"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "One per record."
        },
        {
          "id": "cb14-l2-e2",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What does the report show for LINUS T.?",
          "options": [
            "$9.99",
            "$999",
            "$0.99",
            "$99.90"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "His record holds 0000999: 9.99 dollars."
        },
        {
          "id": "cb14-l2-e3",
          "type": "fill_blank",
          "prompt": "Print the detail line.",
          "code": [
            "           WRITE PRINT-LINE FROM ___."
          ],
          "options": [
            "DETAIL-LINE",
            "CUST-REC",
            "PRINT-LINE",
            "REPORT-FILE"
          ],
          "answer": "DETAIL-LINE",
          "explanation": "The line built in WORKING-STORAGE."
        },
        {
          "id": "cb14-l2-e4",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "Why do the balances line up on the right?",
          "options": [
            "Every D-BAL has the same picture and width",
            "The printer aligns them",
            "WRITE adds spaces",
            "Luck"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Fixed fields, fixed columns."
        },
        {
          "id": "cb14-l2-e5",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "In which paragraph is each detail line built?",
          "options": [
            "PRINT-DETAIL, performed for every record",
            "MAIN, once",
            "At STOP RUN",
            "In the FD"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "NOT AT END PERFORM PRINT-DETAIL."
        },
        {
          "id": "cb14-l2-e6",
          "type": "order_lines",
          "prompt": "Put the steps for one record in order.",
          "lines": [
            "           MOVE CUST-NAME TO D-NAME.",
            "           MOVE CUST-BAL TO D-BAL.",
            "           WRITE PRINT-LINE FROM DETAIL-LINE."
          ],
          "answer": [
            "           MOVE CUST-NAME TO D-NAME.",
            "           MOVE CUST-BAL TO D-BAL.",
            "           WRITE PRINT-LINE FROM DETAIL-LINE."
          ],
          "explanation": "Fill the line, then write it."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cb14-l3",
      "title": "Totals",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "At the end of a report come the totals: count the records and add up the amounts while reading, then print a total line after the loop.",
        "Totals need VALUE ZERO, or the first ADD abends with S0C7.",
        "An average is one COMPUTE at the end: TOTAL / COUNT, ROUNDED."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.",
          "       PROGRAM-ID. TOTALS.",
          "       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.",
          "       INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.",
          "       FILE-CONTROL.",
          "           SELECT CUST-FILE ASSIGN TO CUSTOMERS.",
          "           SELECT REPORT-FILE ASSIGN TO PRINTER.",
          "       DATA DIVISION.",
          "       FILE SECTION.",
          "       FD CUST-FILE.",
          "       01 CUST-REC.",
          "          05 CUST-NO      PIC 9(5).",
          "          05 CUST-NAME    PIC X(12).",
          "          05 CUST-CITY    PIC X(10).",
          "          05 CUST-BAL     PIC 9(5)V99.",
          "       FD REPORT-FILE.",
          "       01 PRINT-LINE     PIC X(40).",
          "       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.",
          "       01 EOF-FLAG       PIC X VALUE \"N\".",
          "          88 END-OF-FILE VALUE \"Y\".",
          "       01 CUST-COUNT     PIC 99 VALUE ZERO.",
          "       01 BAL-TOTAL      PIC 9(6)V99 VALUE ZERO.",
          "       01 BAL-AVERAGE    PIC 9(6)V99.",
          "       01 TOTAL-LINE.",
          "          05 T-LABEL      PIC X(10).",
          "          05 T-AMOUNT     PIC $$$,$$9.99.",
          "       PROCEDURE DIVISION.",
          "       MAIN.",
          "           OPEN INPUT CUST-FILE OUTPUT REPORT-FILE.",
          "           PERFORM UNTIL END-OF-FILE",
          "               READ CUST-FILE",
          "                   AT END SET END-OF-FILE TO TRUE",
          "                   NOT AT END",
          "                       ADD 1 TO CUST-COUNT",
          "                       ADD CUST-BAL TO BAL-TOTAL",
          "               END-READ",
          "           END-PERFORM.",
          "           COMPUTE BAL-AVERAGE ROUNDED = BAL-TOTAL / CUST-COUNT.",
          "           MOVE \"TOTAL\" TO T-LABEL.",
          "           MOVE BAL-TOTAL TO T-AMOUNT.",
          "           WRITE PRINT-LINE FROM TOTAL-LINE.",
          "           MOVE \"AVERAGE\" TO T-LABEL.",
          "           MOVE BAL-AVERAGE TO T-AMOUNT.",
          "           WRITE PRINT-LINE FROM TOTAL-LINE.",
          "           CLOSE CUST-FILE REPORT-FILE.",
          "           STOP RUN."
        ],
        "output": [
          "TOTAL      $4,445.35",
          "AVERAGE    $1,111.34"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "cb14-l3-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "When is the total line printed?",
          "options": [
            "After the loop, once all records are read",
            "With every record",
            "Before the first READ",
            "At OPEN"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Only then is the total complete."
        },
        {
          "id": "cb14-l3-e2",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "Why must BAL-TOTAL have VALUE ZERO?",
          "options": [
            "Otherwise it holds spaces and the first ADD abends with S0C7",
            "To print it",
            "Totals need no VALUE",
            "To make it bigger"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "The classic."
        },
        {
          "id": "cb14-l3-e3",
          "type": "fill_blank",
          "prompt": "Count each record.",
          "code": [
            "                       ADD 1 TO ___"
          ],
          "options": [
            "CUST-COUNT",
            "CUST-REC",
            "EOF-FLAG",
            "1"
          ],
          "answer": "CUST-COUNT",
          "explanation": "The counter."
        },
        {
          "id": "cb14-l3-e4",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What's the total of all 4 balances (2500.00 + 1815.36 + 120.00 + 9.99)?",
          "options": [
            "4445.35",
            "4435.35",
            "4445.36",
            "4545.35"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Add them up: 4445.35."
        },
        {
          "id": "cb14-l3-e5",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "Why is the average COMPUTEd after the loop?",
          "options": [
            "The total and the count are only final then",
            "COMPUTE can't be in a loop",
            "It's faster",
            "To save paper"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Compute from the finished numbers."
        },
        {
          "id": "cb14-l3-e6",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What would happen if the file were empty?",
          "options": [
            "CUST-COUNT is 0, and the average divides by zero: S0CB",
            "The average is 0",
            "Nothing",
            "S0C7"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Careful programs check IF CUST-COUNT > 0 first."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}